              "short": "Values from top to bottom are $1.50000$, $1.40000$, $1.41667$, $1.41379$ and $1.41429$.\n\nThe corresponding differences are $0.08579$, $0.01421$, $0.00246$, $0.00042$ and $0.00008$.",
              "worked": "Evaluate from the innermost denominator. Let $D_n$ be the outer denominator when the shorthand has $n$ twos. Each additional level gives $D_{n+1}=2+\\frac{1}{D_n}$.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}\nD_1&=2\\\\\nD_2&=2+\\tfrac12=\\tfrac52\\\\\nD_3&=2+\\tfrac25=\\tfrac{12}{5}\\\\\nD_4&=2+\\tfrac5{12}=\\tfrac{29}{12}\\\\\nD_5&=2+\\tfrac{12}{29}=\\tfrac{70}{29}.\n\\end{align*}$$\n\nFor each truncation, calculate $C_n=1+\\frac{1}{D_n}$. Subtract $1.41421$ from the exact value, take the absolute value and round both table entries to five decimal places.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}\nC_1&=1+\\tfrac12=\\tfrac32=1.50000, & |C_1-1.41421|&=0.08579\\\\\nC_2&=1+\\tfrac25=\\tfrac75=1.40000, & |C_2-1.41421|&=0.01421\\\\\nC_3&=1+\\tfrac5{12}=\\tfrac{17}{12}\\approx1.41667, & |C_3-1.41421|&\\approx0.00246\\\\\nC_4&=1+\\tfrac{12}{29}=\\tfrac{41}{29}\\approx1.41379, & |C_4-1.41421|&\\approx0.00042\\\\\nC_5&=1+\\tfrac{29}{70}=\\tfrac{99}{70}\\approx1.41429, & |C_5-1.41421|&\\approx0.00008.\n\\end{align*}$$\n\n| Continued fraction | Value | $\\sqrt{2}$ reference | Difference |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $[1;2]$ | $1.50000$ | $1.41421$ | $0.08579$ |\n| $[1;2,2]$ | $1.40000$ | $1.41421$ | $0.01421$ |\n| $[1;2,2,2]$ | $1.41667$ | $1.41421$ | $0.00246$ |\n| $[1;2,2,2,2]$ | $1.41379$ | $1.41421$ | $0.00042$ |\n| $[1;2,2,2,2,2]$ | $1.41429$ | $1.41421$ | $0.00008$ |",
